HedgeGuard.setTarget
├── when the caller is not the hedger
│   └── it should revert with OnlyHedger
└── when the caller is the hedger
    ├── when the target is invalid (zero maker, no direction, zero size, zero or inverted prices, zero target id, past expiry)
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidTarget
    └── when the target is valid
        └── it should store the target, overwrite any remaining size and emit TargetSet

HedgeGuard.clearTarget
├── when the caller is not the hedger
│   └── it should revert with OnlyHedger
└── when the caller is the hedger
    └── it should delete the target and emit TargetCleared

HedgeGuard.setOracle
├── when the caller is not the owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when the caller is the owner
    ├── when the feed is zero, or max age is zero, or deviation is zero or above 10000 bps
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidOracleConfig
    └── when the config is valid
        └── it should store the config and emit OracleConfigured

HedgeGuard.setHedger
├── when the caller is not the owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when the caller is the owner
    ├── when the new hedger is zero
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    └── when the new hedger is non-zero
        └── it should rotate the hedger and emit HedgerChanged

HedgeGuard.oraclePriceE8
├── when the feed has 8 decimals
│   └── it should return the answer
├── when the feed has more than 8 decimals
│   └── it should divide down to 8 decimals
└── when the feed has fewer than 8 decimals
    └── it should multiply up to 8 decimals
